        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/765a6552e96e04a199ed8cddd2bb5270eb8eaf37"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 765a6552e96e04a199ed8cddd2bb5270eb8eaf37\nparent 649bc0a645eb127a9b1e6d078f8d129be6380c87\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792039758 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792041635 +0200\n\nlog: escape C1 control characters in messages\n\nLogEscapeMessage escapes bytes below 0x20 and 0x7f, but passes the\nUTF-8 encodings of U+0080 to U+009F (0xC2 0x80 to 0xC2 0x9F), which\ninclude CSI, OSC and DCS. VTE-based terminals, such as GNOME Terminal,\nact on them.\n\nEscape these two-byte sequences as well. 0xC2 is never a continuation\nbyte, so no decoder state is needed, and every other UTF-8 sequence\nstill passes through unaltered.\n",
